Relevant columns and their potential usage
• NOAA_DATA_PLUS.GEO_US_BOUNDARIES.ZIP_CODES  
  – "city": city to be returned in the result set.  
  – "zip_code": 5‑digit postal code to be returned in the result set.  
  – "state_code": two‑letter state abbreviation to be returned in the result set.  
  – "zip_code_geom": polygon geometry that defines the spatial boundary of the ZIP code; needed for the spatial comparison.  

• NOAA_DATA_PLUS.NOAA_HURRICANES.HURRICANES  
  – "name": storm name; filter out blanks / ‘UNNAMED’.  
  – "latitude": storm center latitude.  
  – "longitude": storm center longitude.  
  – "sid": unique storm identifier; useful when de‑duplicating multiple 6‑hourly fixes from the same storm.  
  – "iso_time": timestamp of the fix; may be used later to pick representative points or for extra filters.  

Key condition that will be required later
ST_WITHIN( ST_MAKEPOINT("HUR"."longitude", "HUR"."latitude") ,
           "ZIP"."zip_code_geom" )

Below are 10 step‑by‑step Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that progressively explore the data and show how one would arrive at the final answer.  
All column names are enclosed in double quotes, and each query is preceded by a short description.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Preview basic ZIP‑code information (first 20 rows)
